WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.272
Let's summarize the practical NumPy skills from this module.

00:00:05.272 --> 00:00:11.602
For creation, you should recognize array, arange, linspace, zeros, and ones.

00:00:11.602 --> 00:00:18.227
For structure, you should be comfortable with dtype, shape, ndim, size, reshape, and transpose.

00:00:18.227 --> 00:00:22.577
For selection, know indexing, slicing, Boolean masks, and where.

00:00:22.577 --> 00:00:29.702
For mathematics, understand vectorized operations, universal functions, broadcasting,

00:00:29.702 --> 00:00:32.187
and the basic idea of a dot product.

00:00:32.187 --> 00:00:39.507
For statistical work, be able to calculate mean, median, standard deviation, percentiles,

00:00:39.507 --> 00:00:45.482
and nan-aware summaries. Professional habits are just as important as individual functions.

00:00:45.482 --> 00:00:49.902
Use a fixed seed when reproducibility matters.

00:00:49.902 --> 00:00:52.132
Inspect shape before combining arrays.

00:00:52.132 --> 00:00:55.577
Check dtype when results look strange.

00:00:55.577 --> 00:01:01.642
Investigate outliers instead of deleting them automatically.

00:01:01.642 --> 00:01:05.632
Use copies intentionally when modifying slices.

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:09.532
You do not need to remember every NumPy function from memory.

00:01:09.532 --> 00:01:18.668
You need to recognize the patterns and know how to find the specific function when you need it.
